+FASTQ is read as 4-line records.  If a file ends partway through a record
+(its line count is not a multiple of 4), construction stops with
+`Truncated FASTQ input '<file>' ...` and a nonzero exit code instead of
+building from the incomplete data.  Discard the output directory and fix or
+re-transfer the input.
+
+Reads must use uppercase `A`, `C`, `G`, `N`, `T`.  Since pymsbwt 0.5.0,
+any other symbol (lowercase soft-masking such as `acgt`, IUPAC codes such
+as `R` or `Y`) stops construction with a `ValueError` naming the read,
+position and symbol.  Uppercase soft-masked input and map IUPAC codes to
+`N` before building.  Earlier releases did not check, and such input could
+hang `msbwt cffq` or corrupt memory.
+
