-`--drop-lcp` explicitly produces a reduced MSBWT without the LCP layer
-(LCP-preserving removal is not part of this release — see the
-[LCP Retrofit](LCP-Retrofit) page).
+An LCP layer on the input is carried into the reduced index (since
+pymsbwt 0.5.0).  `--drop-lcp` produces a reduced index without it.  In
+0.4.0 and the Python 2.7 line, removal from an LCP-enabled index needs
+`--drop-lcp`.  See [LCP Retrofit](LCP-Retrofit).
 
